  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Multi-Sector Assistance for Vulnerable, Conflict-Affected Communities in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan remains one of the most complex humanitarian operating environments with deteriorating infrastructure, cumulative effect of long and heavy rainy season and several armed groups still active in various parts of the country. The future of the country remains uncertain and the resulting humanitarian needs unpredictable. Through this project, IOM aims at contributing to prevent, reduce and mitigate protection threats for persons affected by crisis in South Sudan through the provision of multi-sector life-saving humanitarian assistance. In particular, IOM is supporting affected populations through the provision of water, site care and maintenance, as well as enhancing the psychological well-being of affected populations. In addition, IOM is further strengthening the capacity of the humanitarian aid system to provide timely and targeted humanitarian assistance through information management through IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), camp management, management of the shelter and non-food item and water, sanitation and hygiene cluster coordination and the establishment of humanitarian hubs in deep field locations.</narrative>
  </description>
